
What is lambda Expression?
 -It is an anonymous function (Nameless, No return Type, Without modifiers)

The main objective of lambda Expression:
  - to bring benefits of functional programing into java

Very Vary Vary Easy!!!

Example:

   Normal Method:

    public void Test(){
       System.out.println("hallo");
    }

   Lambda Method:

     () -> System.out.println("hallo");


Example2 :

   Normal Method  :

   Public void Test(int a, String b){
      System.out.println(a);
      System.out.println(b);
   }

   Lambda Method:

    (int a, int b) -> System.out.println(a + b);

Example3:

    Normal Method  :

       Public void Test(int n){
          return n*n;
       }

       Lambda Method:

        1) (int n) -> n*n;

        2) (n) -> n*n;

        3) n -> n*n;

Example4:

    Normal Method  :

      public void m1(String s){
         return s.length();
      }

    Lambda Method:

        s -> s.length();

1
    n -> return n*n; --> invalid
    n -> {return n*n;};--> valid
    n -> {return n*n}; --> invalid
    n -> {n*n;}; --> invalid
    n -> n*n; --> valid

    Note : - without curly braces we cannot use return keyword. compiler will consider return value automatically
           - Within curly braces if we wont to return some value compulsory we should use return statement.
